# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: TubeSearch.
Package: TubeSearch
Section: Video
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport, Reel (>= 0.1.27)
Components: Apps.Video.!TubeSearch (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-tubesearch
Description: Search and browse YouTube, and play videos in Reel
 Shows YouTube search results, channels and related videos with their
 pictures, and plays the video you click in Reel, using the Pi's
 hardware decoder. It answers YouTube's challenges itself with QuickJS
 and yt-dlp's solver scripts. Needs AcornSSL (RISC OS 5.28 or later)
 and a 32K or 16M colour desktop. Not affiliated with YouTube or
 Google.
 .
 This is a release candidate.
Build-Map: !TubeSearch -> Apps/Video/!TubeSearch
Build-Notice: TubeSearch, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-tubesearch/releases
 .
 TubeSearch is under the MIT licence. It includes QuickJS (MIT), yt-dlp's
 ejs scripts (Unlicense), meriyah (ISC) and astring (MIT). Licences
 follow.
